{"docs":[{"description":"Larger agent systems built by combining simpler patterns, such as a research system with a lead agent and parallel searchers.","slug":"advanced","title":"Advanced Architectures"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"Treat an agent workflow as a graph of nodes, edges and prompts, and search that space with an evaluator, as GPTSwarm, AFlow and MASS do.","slug":"agent-graph-optimization","title":"Agent-Graph Optimization"},{"cluster":"security","description":"Give each agent its own identity and short-lived, task-scoped credentials so delegation narrows authority and actions are attributable.","slug":"agent-identity-scoped-credentials","title":"Agent Identity and Scoped Credentials"},{"cluster":"security","description":"Sign, pin and allowlist the models, tools, protocol servers and prompts an agent loads, and keep a way to revoke any of them at once.","slug":"agentic-supply-chain","title":"Agentic Supply Chain Integrity"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"Wrap a specialist agent as a tool, so a calling agent can hand it one bounded task and keep control.","slug":"agents-as-tools","title":"Agents as Tools"},{"description":"Common mistakes in agent systems, how to recognise them, and how to avoid them.","slug":"antipatterns","title":"Anti-Patterns"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"A language model enhanced with retrieval, tools and memory that it uses actively, described by Anthropic as the basic building block of agentic systems.","slug":"augmented-llm","title":"The Augmented LLM"},{"cluster":"product","description":"A six-level scale for how much an agent may decide alone, chosen per kind of action from risk, not from model capability.","slug":"autonomy-ladder","title":"The Autonomy Ladder"},{"cluster":"topologies","description":"Independent specialists work on one problem through a shared workspace; a control step picks who contributes next.","slug":"blackboard","title":"Blackboard"},{"cluster":"classical","description":"Give each agent, tenant or dependency its own bounded resource pool, so a fault or overload in one stays out of the others.","slug":"bulkhead-isolation","title":"Bulkhead Isolation"},{"cluster":"operations-reliability","description":"Release a changed prompt or model to a small share of live traffic, or to a copy of it, and compare it with the current version before promoting.","slug":"canary-and-shadow-prompts","title":"Canary and Shadow Deployment for Prompts and Models"},{"cluster":"upkeep","description":"What a card of this node must hold, stated so that tasks can follow it and a check can test it.","slug":"card-format","title":"Card format"},{"cluster":"upkeep","description":"Compare one card with the public sources it cites and propose the result.","slug":"check-a-card-against-its-sources","title":"Check a card against its sources"},{"description":"Established software patterns, such as the saga, applied to agent workflows.","slug":"classical","title":"Classical Foundations"},{"description":"Ideas from cognitive science, such as self-monitoring, turned into agent patterns.","slug":"cognitive-behavioral","title":"Cognitive & Behavioral"},{"cluster":"cognitive-behavioral","description":"Choose an agent's next task from novelty or learning progress instead of a fixed task list, as in Voyager's automatic curriculum.","slug":"curiosity-driven-curriculum","title":"Curiosity-Driven Curriculum"},{"description":"How agents find and use the right information, and how to measure whether they did.","slug":"data-retrieval","title":"Data & Retrieval"},{"cluster":"advanced","description":"Split a question into parts, search them in parallel, combine the findings and check that every claim has a source.","slug":"deep-research-loop","title":"The Deep Research Loop"},{"cluster":"security","description":"Keep the model that can act away from untrusted text: a tool-less model reads it, and plain code passes results between them.","slug":"dual-llm-pattern","title":"Dual-LLM Pattern"},{"cluster":"evaluation-testing","description":"Read traces, write open notes, then group them into a failure taxonomy, so the categories come from the data.","slug":"error-analysis-coding","title":"Error Analysis by Open and Axial Coding"},{"description":"Human control over autonomous systems, and their effects on people and the environment.","slug":"ethics","title":"Ethics & Sustainability"},{"description":"How to test agents and measure whether they work.","slug":"evaluation-testing","title":"Evaluation & Testing"},{"cluster":"cognitive-behavioral","description":"Improve prompts by keeping a population, letting an LLM mutate and recombine it, scoring on a training set and keeping the fittest.","slug":"evolutionary-prompt-search","title":"Evolutionary Prompt Search"},{"cluster":"operations-reliability","description":"Classify each failure, retry short faults with limits, switch route for lasting ones, and report reduced results honestly.","slug":"exception-handling-and-recovery","title":"Exception Handling and Recovery"},{"description":"The basic building blocks of agents, such as loops, tools and ways of combining model calls.","slug":"foundational","title":"Foundational"},{"description":"Open research questions about agents, with what is known and what is not.","slug":"future","title":"Future Research"},{"cluster":"reference-architectures","description":"A simulated character with a full memory record, reflection over it, and plans drawn from both, so it stays consistent over days.","slug":"generative-agents","title":"Generative Agents"},{"cluster":"cognitive-behavioral","description":"Write agent requirements as Given/When/Then scenarios and run each as a repeatable evaluation.","slug":"given-when-then-agent-specs","title":"Given/When/Then Agent Specs"},{"cluster":"cognitive-behavioral","description":"Specialist modules share one workspace, with specialised processors around it, as in Global Workspace Theory.","slug":"global-workspace-blackboard","title":"Global Workspace as Blackboard"},{"cluster":"reasoning-decision","description":"Give an agent a goal with checkable criteria, then monitor its progress and decide to continue, re-plan or stop.","slug":"goal-setting-and-monitoring","title":"Goal Setting and Monitoring"},{"cluster":"evaluation-testing","description":"Store a known-good agent run as a test case and replay it on each change; Google's ADK and Anthropic describe tolerant ways to compare the results.","slug":"golden-trajectory-snapshots","title":"Golden Trajectories and Snapshot Tests"},{"description":"Records, rules and checks that make agent actions accountable.","slug":"governance","title":"Governance & Accountability"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"Model LLM reasoning as a graph of thoughts and dependencies, so thoughts can be combined and refined, not only branched.","slug":"graph-of-thoughts","title":"Graph of Thoughts"},{"cluster":"sdlc","description":"An agent works on its own branch and cannot approve or merge; a named human decides what reaches the main branch.","slug":"human-only-merge-gate","title":"Human-Only Merge Gate"},{"cluster":"evaluation-testing","description":"Attach a stable idempotency key to each side-effecting call so a retried or replayed request is executed once, as Stripe and Temporal describe.","slug":"idempotent-agent-actions","title":"Idempotency Keys for Agent Actions"},{"cluster":"governance","description":"An append-only, hash-linked record of every important agent action, so what happened can be rebuilt and checked.","slug":"immutable-audit-log","title":"Tamper-Evident Agent Audit Log"},{"cluster":"evaluation-testing","description":"Measure an automated judge against human labels before trusting its verdicts, and audit it for position, verbosity and self-enhancement bias.","slug":"judge-calibration","title":"Judge Calibration"},{"cluster":"upkeep","description":"The decision that each card says one thing under each heading, in one sentence.","slug":"keep-cards-short","title":"Keep cards short"},{"cluster":"ethics","description":"Two conditions for real human control: the system responds to relevant human reasons, and its actions trace to a person who understands it.","slug":"meaningful-human-control","title":"Meaningful Human Control"},{"description":"How agents remember, forget and turn past work into reusable skills.","slug":"memory-cognition","title":"Memory & Cognition"},{"cluster":"security","description":"Treat writes to agent memory and retrieval stores as untrusted: validate, attribute, segment and expire entries, following OWASP ASI06.","slug":"memory-context-poisoning","title":"Memory and Context Poisoning Defense"},{"cluster":"cognitive-behavioral","description":"A meta level watches how sure the agent is while it works and decides to continue, retry or abstain.","slug":"metacognitive-monitoring","title":"Metacognitive Monitoring and Control"},{"cluster":"topologies","description":"Several model instances propose answers, read one another's responses and revise over rounds; a judge or convergence ends the debate.","slug":"multi-agent-debate","title":"Multi-Agent Debate"},{"description":"Running agents in production, including handling failures, controlling cost and watching behaviour.","slug":"operations-reliability","title":"Operations & Reliability"},{"cluster":"product","description":"Charge for achieved outcomes such as a resolved conversation instead of seats or usage, which requires agreeing criteria for the outcome upfront.","slug":"outcome-based-pricing","title":"Outcome-Based Pricing"},{"cluster":"security","description":"OWASP's list of ten security risks for agents that act, a shared vocabulary for threat models and security reviews.","slug":"owasp-agentic-top-10","title":"OWASP Top 10 for Agentic Applications"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"Run independent subtasks at once and combine the results, either by splitting the work or by running the same task several times.","slug":"parallelization","title":"Parallelization"},{"cluster":"evaluation-testing","description":"Score an agent by the probability that all k repeated trials of a task succeed, rather than at least one.","slug":"pass-hat-k","title":"Pass^k Reliability"},{"cluster":"sdlc","description":"The agent researches and proposes a plan without editing source; a person approves, changes or rejects it before edits start.","slug":"plan-approval-gate","title":"Plan Approval Gate"},{"description":"Product decisions for agents, such as how much an agent may do on its own.","slug":"product","title":"Product Practice"},{"cluster":"operations-reliability","description":"Put the stable prompt prefix first and variable content last so provider prompt caches can reuse it on later requests.","slug":"prompt-caching-layout","title":"Prompt-Caching Layout"},{"description":"Shared formats and addresses that let agents, tools and organisations work together.","slug":"protocols","title":"Protocols & Interop"},{"cluster":"upkeep","slug":"publish-gate","title":"Publish gate"},{"description":"How agents set goals, decide what to do next and know when to stop.","slug":"reasoning-decision","title":"Reasoning & Decision"},{"cluster":"evaluation-testing","description":"Record real model responses in one test run and replay them from a cassette on later runs, so tests run offline and repeat exactly.","slug":"record-replay-cassettes","title":"Record–Replay for Agent Tests"},{"description":"Complete agent designs that combine several patterns into one working system.","slug":"reference-architectures","title":"Reference Architectures"},{"cluster":"product","description":"Separate deflection, containment and resolution, and state how 'resolved' is verified, as Intercom, Zendesk and Sierra define it.","slug":"resolution-rate-metrics","title":"Resolution, Containment and Deflection Metrics"},{"cluster":"data-retrieval","description":"Measure whether retrieval found the right material separately from whether the answer used it faithfully.","slug":"retrieval-evaluation","title":"Retrieval Evaluation"},{"cluster":"ethics","description":"Design agents so a human stop is honoured and the agent does not learn to avoid or seek interruption.","slug":"safe-interruptibility","title":"Safe Interruptibility"},{"cluster":"classical","description":"Give each important agent step an undo action, so a failed multi-step run can be rolled back instead of left half done.","slug":"saga-for-agents","title":"Saga for Agent Workflows"},{"description":"Building software with agents through phases, approval gates and reviews.","slug":"sdlc","title":"Agentic SDLC"},{"description":"Threats to agents, and the designs that defend against them.","slug":"security","title":"Security"},{"cluster":"product","description":"Run an agent on live work with its side effects suppressed, then compare its proposed actions with what people actually did.","slug":"shadow-mode-rollout","title":"Shadow-Mode Rollout"},{"cluster":"memory-cognition","description":"Store verified procedures so an agent's skills build up across tasks instead of being rediscovered every run.","slug":"skill-library","title":"Skill-Library Compounding"},{"cluster":"specs","description":"Agents optimise the criterion you wrote, not the result you meant; the gap between the two is where failures hide.","slug":"specification-gaming","title":"Specification Gaming"},{"description":"How to state what an agent should do when its behaviour is not fully predictable.","slug":"specs","title":"Specs & Requirements"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"Express an agent as nodes, edges and shared state run in super-steps with checkpoints, as in LangGraph and Google's Pregel model.","slug":"state-graph-agents","title":"Agent as State Graph"},{"cluster":"protocols","description":"A well-known URI where a system publishes its energy and carbon figures, and reads its peers' figures as input to its decisions.","slug":"sustainability-signal-plane","title":"Sustainability Signal Plane"},{"cluster":"upkeep","description":"Open each source of one card, confirm that it still says what the card says, and record the date.","slug":"task-recheck-sources","title":"Re-check the sources of a card"},{"cluster":"upkeep","description":"Tell the node about a source address that fails, with the name of the card that cites it.","slug":"task-report-a-broken-link","title":"Report a source that no longer answers"},{"cluster":"foundational","description":"Define in advance each way an agent loop ends, such as a final answer, a turn limit, or a pause for human input.","slug":"termination-conditions","title":"Termination and Exit Conditions"},{"cluster":"operations-reliability","description":"Set how much reasoning a model spends per task class before the call, using effort levels and thinking settings that providers document.","slug":"thinking-budget-control","title":"Thinking-Budget Control"},{"description":"Ways for several agents to work together, such as a shared workspace or a hierarchy.","slug":"topologies","title":"Multi-Agent Topologies"},{"cluster":"evaluation-testing","description":"Grade the end state an agent produced and the path it took as two separate questions, each with a suitable grader.","slug":"trajectory-vs-outcome-evals","title":"Trajectory and Outcome Evaluation"},{"cluster":"antipatterns","description":"An agent loop with no step limit, no budget and no independent exit test runs until money, patience or the platform stops it.","slug":"unbounded-agent-loops","title":"Unbounded Loops"},{"description":"The node's own work on one board: the decision on card length, the card format, the gate and the open tasks.","slug":"upkeep","title":"Upkeep"},{"cluster":"future","description":"Open question: can weaker judges, human or model, reliably oversee agents stronger than themselves? What is known and what is not.","slug":"weak-to-strong-oversight","title":"Weak-to-Strong Oversight"}],"terms":{"10":[2,3,18,40,44,45],"15":[17],"1980":[8],"1987